THOUGHT: Now I understand the vulnerability. The bug is in `fwupd_guid_from_string` in `libfwupd/fwupd-common.c`. The vulnerable code uses `&&` instead of `||`:

```c
if (strlen(split[0]) != 8 && strlen(split[1]) != 4 && strlen(split[2]) != 4 &&
    strlen(split[3]) != 4 && strlen(split[4]) != 12) {
```

This means the length check only fails if ALL parts have wrong lengths. If only ONE part has the wrong length (e.g., split[0] is not 8 chars), the check passes and the code proceeds to parse the GUID, reading beyond the buffer.

The crash is in `fu_coswid_firmware_write` calling `fwupd_guid_from_string`. Let me look at the current code in the repo to see the vulnerable version and understand how the GUID is used in the write path.
