    return (uint8_t)item->data.uint.value;
}
```

This reads 1 byte. `cbor_get_uint16` reads 2 bytes:
```c
uint16_t cbor_get_uint16(const cbor_item_t *item) {
    return (uint16_t)item->data.uint.value;
}
```

So a "READ 2" could be from `cbor_get_uint16`. Let me look at where `cbor_get_uint16` is used:

In `fu_coswid_read_version_scheme`:
